# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. `.env` is git-ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Database (PostgreSQL) -------------------------------------------------
# Neon, Supabase, Vercel Postgres or a local server all work.
# Leave this OUT entirely to run the public site on its bundled content —
# accounts and the admin area stay switched off until it is set.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE?sslmode=require"

# --- NextAuth --------------------------------------------------------------
# Required. Generate one with:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
NEXTAUTH_SECRET="replace-with-a-long-random-string"

# The public URL of the site. Both values below are for local development.
#
# IN PRODUCTION both must be:  https://www.christmysooncomingkingministry.org
# With `www` — the apex redirects to it — and no trailing slash.
#
# Leaving these at localhost on a deployed site is not a cosmetic fault. It
# sends canonical links, og:image and the sitemap to a machine nobody else can
# reach, so link previews come up blank and search engines index nothing; it
# points NextAuth's sign-in redirect at localhost; and it prints event check-in
# QR codes that scan to a dead address (see lib/qr.ts).
NEXTAUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Used in metadata, sitemap.xml, robots.txt and the check-in QR codes.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are inlined into the bundle at build time, so changing
# this on the host does nothing until you trigger a fresh deploy.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# --- Search engine verification (optional) ---------------------------------
# Only needed if you verify ownership by meta tag. Verifying by DNS record
# instead is better — it covers every subdomain and survives a redesign — in
# which case leave both of these blank.
#
#   Google:  https://search.google.com/search-console  → the "HTML tag" method,
#            copy only the content="..." value, not the whole tag.
#   Bing:    https://www.bing.com/webmasters
GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=""
BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=""

# --- Google sign-in (optional) ---------------------------------------------
# Leave both blank to hide the "Continue with Google" button entirely.
# Authorised redirect URI: <your site>/api/auth/callback/google
# In production: https://www.christmysooncomingkingministry.org/api/auth/callback/google
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# --- First admin account (optional, used by `npm run db:seed`) -------------
# Set these once, run the seed, then remove them from your .env.
SEED_ADMIN_EMAIL=""
SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD=""
SEED_ADMIN_NAME="Ministry Admin"

# --- Scheduled jobs (optional but recommended) ---------------------------
# Enables /api/cron (chat retention, orphaned uploads, event reminders).
# Generate:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# Then call hourly:
#   curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $CRON_SECRET" \
#     https://www.christmysooncomingkingministry.org/api/cron
CRON_SECRET=""

# --- File uploads ----------------------------------------------------------
# Two drivers, chosen automatically — see lib/storage.ts.
#
#   Local disk    — the default. Fine for `npm start` on a server or a VPS.
#                   Set UPLOAD_DIR to move it; blank uses ./.uploads .
#
#   Vercel Blob   — used automatically when BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN is present.
#                   REQUIRED ON VERCEL. A serverless filesystem is read-only
#                   apart from /tmp, and /tmp does not survive between
#                   invocations — so without this, every uploaded photo,
#                   announcement design and chat attachment is lost as soon as
#                   the function that wrote it goes away.
#
#                   Vercel sets this variable for you the moment you attach a
#                   Blob store: Storage → Create → Blob → Connect to project.
UPLOAD_DIR=""
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# --- Two-factor authentication -------------------------------------------
# Encrypts stored TOTP secrets. Falls back to NEXTAUTH_SECRET if unset, but
# set it separately: rotating NEXTAUTH_SECRET would otherwise make every
# stored secret undecryptable and lock your staff out.
# Generate:  node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
TWO_FACTOR_KEY=""

# --- AI (optional, and free) ---------------------------------------------
# Powers "Ask this sermon". Leave all of this blank and the feature still
# works: people get the parts of the sermon that match their question, found
# by search. A model only adds a short written summary on top.
#
# THE RULE: only *published sermon transcripts* are ever sent to an outside
# model. Prayer requests, pastoral care requests, chat and members-only posts
# are never sent anywhere — that is enforced in code (see lib/ai.ts), not by
# policy. Free tiers train on what you send them and humans may read it.
#
# Pick one:
#
#   gemini  — Google's free tier. Best quality for nothing. No card needed.
#             Key from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#             Check your live limits at https://aistudio.google.com/rate-limit
#   groq    — Also free, very fast, open models.
#             Key from https://console.groq.com/keys
#   ollama  — Runs on your own machine. Free AND private, but needs a computer
#             with enough RAM that stays on. https://ollama.com
#
AI_PROVIDER=""

# For AI_PROVIDER="gemini"
GEMINI_API_KEY=""
# Optional. Google renames models often — if answers stop coming, check the
# model list and set this. Default: gemini-2.5-flash-lite
GEMINI_MODEL=""

# For AI_PROVIDER="groq"
GROQ_API_KEY=""
GROQ_MODEL=""

# For AI_PROVIDER="ollama" — e.g. http://localhost:11434
OLLAMA_URL=""
OLLAMA_MODEL=""
